charge.t.sol
├── when the caller is not the relayer
│   └── it should revert with the {OnlyRelayer} error
└── when the caller is the relayer
    ├── given the subscription is not registered
    │   └── it should revert with the {SubscriptionNull} error
    └── given the subscription is registered
        ├── given the subscription is revoked
        │   └── it should revert with the {SubscriptionRevoked} error
        └── given the subscription is not revoked
            ├── given all cycles have been charged
            │   └── it should revert with the {SubscriptionEnded} error
            └── given cycles remain to be charged
                ├── when the next cycle is not due
                │   └── it should revert with the {CycleNotDue} error (this is also the double-charge guard)
                └── when the next cycle is due
                    ├── given the {Space} has not approved the module for the cycle amount
                    │   └── it should revert
                    └── given the {Space} has approved the module for the cycle amount
                        ├── it should bump the charged-cycle counter (the next cycle cursor)
                        ├── it should transfer the relayer-supplied amount from the {Space} to the treasury
                        ├── it should emit the {SubscriptionCharged} event
                        ├── when the price changes between cycles
                        │   └── it should charge each cycle at the relayer-supplied amount
                        └── when the subscription is in arrears
                            └── it should allow consecutive charges to catch up, strictly in order
